      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:QuadrArg">Quadr Arg</ref> 2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Quadr Arg 2" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="532" ed="#liebermann"/>Cnudus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.9"/> iste, Daciæ simul<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.10"/> et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.i"/> Norwegiæ princeps, cum regnum etiam Angliæ suis laudibus adiecisset, non se ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.11"/> tyrannum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.12"/> aut portentorum aliquid exhibere uoluit, sed beata mentis placiditate diram cupiditatis et malorum feditatem continentiæ salutaris gratia mitigauit, tanto sibi subditos ampliori dilectione celebrans, quanto eos in patriæ defensionibus præsenserat acriores.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 532 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.i" n="i" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">532</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Cnut beherrschte England früher als Norwegen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnut ruled England earlier than Norway</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">532</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cnuthus <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi> (<hi rend="italic">stets</hi>)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnuthus Hk (always)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">532</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">simu <hi rend="italic">T; fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">simu T; missing in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">532</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">532</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tir. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tir. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrArg_2.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verfasser stellt sich offenbar vor, Cnut habe England erworben, nachdem er König von Dänemark und Norwegen geworden war: letzteres irrig. Vielleicht benutzte er nur I Cn Pr eigener Übersetzung; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Cnut 3a. 5a. 7a. 10a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The author evidently imagines that Cnut acquired England after he had become king of Denmark and Norway: the latter is wrong. Perhaps he used only I Cn Pr in his own translation; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Cnut 3a. 5a. 7a. 10a</seg></note>
      </div>
